WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.125 --> 00:00:04.708
(upbeat music)

00:00:11.629 --> 00:00:13.112
- [Darren] A lot of people's
reactions when we told

00:00:13.112 --> 00:00:15.384
them that we were going to go
basically to the North Pole

00:00:15.384 --> 00:00:17.165
to ride mountain bikes were,

00:00:17.165 --> 00:00:19.224
are you bringing ice tires?

00:00:19.224 --> 00:00:20.973
'Cause most people
think, in the North Pole,

00:00:20.973 --> 00:00:23.459
they're like, it's going to
be cold and full of snow.

00:00:23.459 --> 00:00:24.600
They don't really realize that

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:27.433
there's an arctic desert up there.

00:00:34.369 --> 00:00:35.491
My name is Darren Berrecloth.

00:00:35.491 --> 00:00:37.283
I'm from Banker Island, British Columbia,

00:00:37.283 --> 00:00:41.763
and I'm a professional
mountain bike free-rider.

00:00:41.763 --> 00:00:44.397
Free-riding is all about
picking your own line,

00:00:44.397 --> 00:00:46.221
and being free to interpret the mountains

00:00:46.221 --> 00:00:48.554
in any way that you see fit.

00:00:51.384 --> 00:00:54.968
- Thinking about starting
on the horizon right there;

00:00:54.968 --> 00:00:58.135
it'll be like a drop up onto a rock slab.

00:00:58.135 --> 00:00:59.683
- [Darren] The reason that
we chose Axel Heiberg Island

00:00:59.683 --> 00:01:01.987
was because the lines were massive.

00:01:01.987 --> 00:01:05.208
It trumped anything that
we ever ridden before,

00:01:05.208 --> 00:01:08.941
in terms of height and just sheer scale.

00:01:08.941 --> 00:01:09.774
- [Speaker 1] Alright, boys.

00:01:09.774 --> 00:01:10.607
- [Speaker 2] Alright.

00:01:10.607 --> 00:01:12.524
- Yeah, boys. Epic time.

00:01:16.387 --> 00:01:18.019
- [Darren] One of the hardest
parts about that whole trip,

00:01:18.019 --> 00:01:20.035
was just it's remoteness and

00:01:20.035 --> 00:01:22.785
how far it was from civilization.

00:01:24.152 --> 00:01:26.486
If something goes wrong, we
were about 12 hours away,

00:01:26.486 --> 00:01:31.236
in best case scenario, from
any hospital or serious help.

00:01:45.784 --> 00:01:47.671
- [Darren] The landscape
up in the high arctic,

00:01:47.671 --> 00:01:49.731
it was just, it was breathtaking.

00:01:49.731 --> 00:01:53.877
Standing at the top of the
line just soaking it all in.

00:01:53.877 --> 00:01:56.044
It's a pretty rad feeling.

00:01:57.077 --> 00:01:58.700
One thing that's amazing
about mountain biking

00:01:58.700 --> 00:02:01.005
is the fact that you can take it anywhere.

00:02:01.005 --> 00:02:02.508
You can climb mountains with it;

00:02:02.508 --> 00:02:04.227
you can descend mountains with it;

00:02:04.227 --> 00:02:06.572
you can travel long distances with it;

00:02:06.572 --> 00:02:11.459
and you can stuff it in a box
and fly it around the world.

00:02:11.459 --> 00:02:13.933
To go up to the high arctic,

00:02:13.933 --> 00:02:17.238
400 miles south of the North
Pole and ride my bikes,

00:02:17.238 --> 00:02:19.043
it's a pretty amazing thing to do.

00:02:19.043 --> 00:02:22.376
Check that off the bucket list, for sure.

